course: dictionary
lesson: 9790
title: Survivor and surviving through hard times
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A survivor is a person or animal that stays alive after something dangerous, such as an accident, a war, an illness or a disaster. The verb is survive, to stay alive or keep going, so a survivor is the one who did it.
explain: Look at the clues around the word: «After strong hurricanes in the Caribbean, scientists found that survivors had bigger toe pads that grip better.» The hurricanes are the danger, and the survivors are the lizards that lived through the storms.
explain: The second meaning is someone who keeps going strongly through hard times. «After the plague so many workers had died that survivors could ask for higher pay.» The survivors are the workers still alive after the plague, and they used their new strength to win better pay.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. Put "the people still alive after the plague" in place of survivors: the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A survivor is a person or animal that stays alive after something dangerous.
fact: Survive is the verb, survivor is the noun, and survivors is the plural.
fact: A survivor can also be someone who keeps going strongly through hard times.
fact: «The tuatara looks like a lizard but is the last survivor of an ancient group of reptiles.» It lives on cool New Zealand islands and can live over 100 years.
fact: In nature, survival of the fittest means the creatures best suited to their home are the ones that survive.
exercise: «The tuatara is the last survivor of an ancient group of reptiles.» What is the survivor here? | A baby lizard | A cool New Zealand island | *An animal still alive from an ancient group | A rescue team that saves people
exercise: «Birds ate the stick insects that looked least like twigs, so the survivors looked more and more like twigs.» What are the survivors? | *The stick insects that stayed alive | The birds that ate the insects | The twigs in the tree | The scientists who measured them
exercise: Nadia says a survivor is someone who never gets hurt at all. Is she right? | No, a survivor is only a person, never an animal | *No, a survivor stayed alive after danger, or kept going through hard times | Yes, a survivor never gets hurt at all | Yes, a survivor is always a hero with a sword
test: «After the earthquake, rescue teams searched for survivors in the rubble.» What are the survivors? | Teams who dig in the rubble | Buildings that fell down | *People still alive after the earthquake | Earthquakes that happen at night
test: «Pointing to one lucky person against the evidence is sometimes called the survivor story.» What does this mean? | A brave hero winning a sword fight | A story about a lizard with big toes | A rescue team's report after a storm | *Using one lucky survivor to ignore the evidence
exam: Which sentence uses survivor with its second meaning, someone who keeps going strongly through hard times? | Birds ate the stick insects that looked least like twigs. | *After the plague, the survivors won higher pay for their work. | The tuatara lives on cool islands near New Zealand. | The survivor of the shipwreck was found on the beach.
